  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The greatest common non-divisor of two positive integers XXX and YYY satisfying X≥5X \\ge 5X≥5 and Y≥5Y \\ge 5Y≥5, denoted gcnd(X,Y)\\text{gcnd}(X, Y)gcnd(X,Y), is defined to be the largest positive integer ZZZ satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\nZ≤XZ \\le XZ≤X **or** Z≤YZ \\le YZ≤Y, and\nXXX is not a multiple of ZZZ **and** YYY is not a multiple of ZZZ.\nIt can be proved that as long as XXX and YYY are both ≥5\\ge 5≥5, gcnd(X,Y)\\text{gcnd}(X, Y)gcnd(X,Y) always exists.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN, such that 5≤Ai≤1075 \\le A_i \\le 10^75≤Ai​≤107 for each 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N. Your task is to compute the maximum gcnd\\text{gcnd}gcnd of some two elements of the array.\n\nThat is, across all pairs of indices (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) satisfying 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N, compute the maximum possible value of gcnd(Ai,Aj)\\text{gcnd}(A_i, A_j)gcnd(Ai​,Aj​).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the maximum possible value of gcnd(Ai,Aj)\\text{gcnd}(A_i, A_j)gcnd(Ai​,Aj​) across all 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "5≤Ai≤1075 \\le A_i \\le 10^75≤Ai​≤107",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n8 5\n3\n6 6 6\n4\n8 9 8 8",
        "output": "7\n5\n7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only choice is to compute gcnd(8,5)\\text{gcnd}(8, 5)gcnd(8,5), since there are only two elements in the array.\nIt can be verified that gcnd(8,5)=7\\text{gcnd}(8, 5) = 7gcnd(8,5)=7, because 777 divides neither 555 nor 888, and no larger integer has this property.\nTest case 222: All the elements are equal to 666, so the answer is gcnd(6,6)\\text{gcnd}(6, 6)gcnd(6,6), which can be verified to be 555.\nTest case 333: One optimal choice is to choose i=1i = 1i=1 and j=4j = 4j=4, to obtain gcnd(A1,A4)=gcnd(8,8)=7\\text{gcnd}(A_1, A_4) = \\text{gcnd}(8, 8) = 7gcnd(A1​,A4​)=gcnd(8,8)=7.\nIt can be proved that no other pair of elements in the array has a larger gcnd\\text{gcnd}gcnd value."
      }
